Machine Learning
Supervised Learning 
  Learns A to B OR Input to Output Mappings
  EX: 
    Input (A): Email
    Output (B): Spam? (0/1)
    Application: Spam Filtering 

    Input (A): Audo
    Output (B): Text Transcipts
    Application: Speech Recognition 

    Input (A): English
    Output (B): Chinese
    Application:  Machine Translation

    Input (A): AD, User Info
    Output (B): Click? (0/1)
    Application:  Online Advertising

    Input (A): Image, radar info
    Output (B): Position of other cars
    Application:  Self-driving Car

    Input (A): Image of Phone 
    Output (B): Defect? (0/1)
    Application:  Visual Inspection

    Input (A): Sequence of Words
    Output (B): Predicts the next word in the sequence
    Application:  Chatbot (LLM)

Large Language Model (LLM)
  Built using supervised learning (A->B) to repeatedly predict the next word
  EX: 
  Give AI model the sentance: "My favorite drink is lychee bubble tea." 
    Input (A): My favorite drink 
    Output (B): is

    Input (A): My favorite drink is 
    Output (B): lychee

    Input (A): My favorite drink is lychee 
    Output (B): bubble

    Input (A): My favorite drink is lychee bubble
    Output (B): tea
When training a very large AI system on a lot of data (hundreds of billions of words), we get a Large Language Model (LLM) like ChatFPT. 
It can seem limiting, but with the right applicable scenario it is very powerful. 
